WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:06.930
Adopting liquid cooling isn't just about
the technology itself.

2
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:13.216
It's about planning for operations, vendor
readiness, and long-term strategic impact

3
00:00:13.216 --> 00:00:14.930
across the organization.

4
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:20.644
Deployment begins with physical layout,
racks, piping, and containment systems

5
00:00:20.644 --> 00:00:22.930
must be carefully designed.

6
00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:27.819
Procurement means sourcing from new
vendors for fluids, hardware, and even

7
00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:30.930
staff training to maintain the systems
properly.

8
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.930
Maintenance is equally critical.

9
00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:37.667
Fluid quality must be tested, filtration
monitored, and predictive analytics

10
00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:41.930
applied to catch problems before they
escalate into downtime.

11
00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:45.930
Strategically, liquid cooling offers
powerful advantages.

12
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:51.263
Lower emissions, reduce energy
consumption, and sustainable end-of-life

13
00:00:51.263 --> 00:00:53.930
practices like fluid recycling.

14
00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:59.385
It directly supports ESG goals and
improves an organization's environmental

15
00:00:59.385 --> 00:00:59.930
footprint.

16
00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:06.041
Organizations adopting liquid cooling
earlier are more likely to meet rising

17
00:01:06.041 --> 00:01:09.930
density and sustainability requirements
ahead of competitors.

18
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:17.430
By engaging with OCP, ASHRAE, and UL,
organizations can help shape global

19
00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.930
standards and accelerate innovation,

20
00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:25.385
while positioning themselves at the
forefront of sustainable data center

21
00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:25.930
design.
